  "analysis_2_exp26_27_split_consistency_P1_2": {
    "root_cause": "Exp 26's reported in_dist_auroc (0.5719) is a 5-fold OOF cross-validated AUROC over all 500 HaluEval samples (from best_layer_probe(), used for layer selection), while its ood_auroc (0.6086) is the held-out performance of a SEPARATE probe trained on a single fixed 75% split (RandomState(42) permutation of 500, tr_idx=idx[:375]). These are two different estimators on different data partitions, not a single consistent train/test split. Exp 27 does not repair this: it introduces a THIRD, independently-seeded 80/20 split (different permutation call, different train fraction) and reports a bootstrap CI centered on ITS OWN point estimate (in-dist=0.5838, ood=0.6477, gap=+0.0639), which is why Exp 27's point estimate does not match Exp 26's reported +0.037 gap.",
    "exp26_reported": {
      "in_dist_auroc_5fold_oof": 0.5718778427550357,
      "ood_auroc_single_split_probe": 0.6085745614035089,
